    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0808" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/3930</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director
                        of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-06-02">June 2, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Grew</hi>: I have read with interest and a
                    growing degree of apprehension the several memoranda and despatches which you
                    have called to my attention recently relative to the apparent growing
                    deterioration in Sino-Soviet relations and the possible development within China
                    of a strong anti-Soviet feeling.</p>
                <p>I would greatly appreciate your recommendations as to what steps could be taken
                    at this time in an effort to improve this unhappy situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
